# 12. XSS AND DOM SAFETY

The current card renderer interpolates product values into dynamic HTML and inline onclick attributes.

Harden the implementation.

Requirements:

- Prefer DOM construction with createElement.
- Use textContent for product names and category text.
- Use setAttribute for validated values.
- Do not interpolate raw product name/image/slug/id into executable inline handlers.
- Avoid event-handler attributes for dynamic content.
- Use event delegation or bound event listeners.
- Validate product links as same-site relative URLs.
- Validate image URLs to allow only safe HTTPS or valid local relative assets.
- Preserve existing Cloudinary product images.
- Use a safe fallback image.
- Avoid injecting untrusted product content through innerHTML.

Static, fixed SVG templates may be used, but never place untrusted product data inside executable markup.

Preserve wishlist action functionality and existing authorization behavior.

Do not change wishlist Firebase rules or data paths.

